<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tempio Malatestiano</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tempio Malatestiano is the cathedral of Rimini, originally the Gothic church of San Francesco. From about 1450 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sigismondo-pandolfo-malatesta">Sigismondo Pandolfo Malatesta</a> had it remodelled by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leon-battista-alberti">Leon Battista Alberti</a>, who designed an unfinished classical façade inspired by Roman triumphal arches, as a monument to himself and Isotta degli Atti. Its interior holds works by Agostino di Duccio and Piero della Francesca.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tempio-malatestiano.jpg" alt="Tempio Malatestiano" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michele1978rimini · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tempio_Malatestiano_Rimini.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
